+**Signs and symptoms:** sweating and fatigue, palpitations, tremor, anxiety, hunger, dizziness and weakness, confusion. Severe cases can cause seizures and coma.
+
+**Hypoglycaemic unawareness:** low glucose without symptoms. It is uncommon, and repeated minor episodes can lead to it.
+
+**Common causes:** missed meals, exercise, alcohol, increasing insulin or sulfonylureas too quickly, worsening kidney function, and injecting insulin into new sites after previously injecting into areas of lipohypertrophy.
